@startuml
title Flows: Sentinel Automation vs Governed API Task Creation

skinparam backgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #444444
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #ffffff
  BoxBorderColor #888888
  BoxBackgroundColor #f8f8f8
}

== Sentinel Automation ==
participant "Telemetry Emitter" as Emit
participant "OTLP Collector" as Coll
participant "Sentinel Worker" as Sen
participant "Rule Engine" as Rule
participant "App Services" as App
participant "Domain" as Dom
database "DB" as DB
participant "API/UI (notify/review)" as Surf

Emit -> Coll : OTLP log/trace\n(messageTemplate + attrs)
Coll -> Sen : Export batch
Sen -> Rule : Evaluate(event)
Rule --> Sen : Match? + TaskTemplate
Sen -> App : CreateTaskFromAutomation(template, context)
App -> Dom : Validate & build Task (source=Sentinel)
Dom --> App : Task entity
App -> DB : Persist
DB --> App : Ack
App --> Sen : TaskId/status
Sen -> Surf : Notify (webhook/signalR)\n(optional for review)

== Governed API Task Creation ==
actor User
participant "UI (Blazor)" as UI
participant "API (REST/JWT)" as API

User -> UI : Request create task
UI -> API : POST /projects/{id}/tasks\nBearer JWT
API -> API : Validate token + model
API -> App : CreateTaskCommand(dto)
App -> Dom : Validate invariants
Dom --> App : Task entity
App -> DB : Persist
DB --> App : Ack
App --> API : TaskDto
API --> UI : 201 Created
UI --> User : Render task

note over Sen, API
  Both flows converge through App/Domain\n  ensuring domain rules and provenance\n  are enforced consistently.
end note

@enduml
